lue "CCS"} "Cross Country Skiing"] "\n" [:option {:value "FSK"} "Figure Skating"] "\n" [:option {:value "IHO"} "Ice Hockey"] "\n" [:option {:value "MSP"} "Military Ski Patrol"] "\n" [:option {:value "NCB"} "Nordic Combined"] "\n" [:option {:value "SJP"} "Ski Jumping"]]] [:script {} "$('#sports_in_same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/32/sports/'+$('#sports_in_same_games_select').val()})"] [:form {:id "other_games_form", :class "form-inline", :style "display: inline", :method "get"} [:select {:name "year", :id "sport_in_other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "Speed Skating in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "29"} "1924 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "30"} "1928 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "31"} "1932 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "33"} "1948 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "34"} "1952 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "35"} "1956 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "36"} "1960 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "37"} "1964 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "38"} "1968 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "39"} "1972 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "40"} "1976 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "41"} "1980 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "42"} "1984 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "43"} "1988 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "44"} "1992 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "45"} "1994 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "46"} "1998 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "47"} "2002 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "49"} "2006 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "57"} "2010 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "66"} "2012 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "58"} "2014 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "68"} "2016 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "60"} "2018 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "70"} "2020 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "62"} "2022 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "73"} "2024 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "72"} "2026 Winter Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/SSK'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Speed Skating at the 1936 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "11 – 14 February 1936"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "4"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/38"} "Olympia-Eissportplatz am Rießersee, Garmisch-Partenkirchen"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "The speed skating events of the 1936 Winter Olympics were set on the " [:a {:href "/venues/38"} "Rießersee"] ", a small lake to the southwest of Garmisch. The lake also hosted a few " [:a {:href "/results/20077"} "hockey"] " matches (two rinks were situated on the inside of the skating rink), and the demonstration sport of " [:a {:href "/editions/32/sports/IST"} "eisstockschießen"] ", a sport with similarities to curling. The newly-built " [:a {:href "/venues/39"} "Olympic bobsleigh course"] " ran alongside the south side of the Rießersee. The Eissportplatz featured a stand with room for 2000 spectators, including 300 seats. Separate radio booths were present, as well as a moveable camera tower. Garmisch had seen skating competitions since the early 20th century, and had organized the German championships on a number of occasions. The 1935 championships had been held on the Rießersee, with Willy Sandtner as the champion."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Olympic speed skating programme was spread out over four days for the first time, instead of two days in the previous Olympics. Sixteen (16) countries participated in the events, with Australia and Czechoslovakia present for the first time. Norway dominated the races, taking all gold medals and six of the 12 medals. " [:a {:href "/athletes/83820"} "Ivar Ballangrud"] " was the star of the Games with three gold medals, tying " [:a {:href "/athletes/98260"} "Clas Thunberg"] "’s 1924 record. The Finn’s overall Olympic medal tally is slightly better than that of Ballangrud, however. The North Americans, which had dominated the " [:a {:href "/editions/31/sports/SSK"} "1932 Olympics"] ", now had to content themselves with " [:a {:href "/results/989"} "a single medal"] ". Canada’s presence was almost compromised by lack of funds, and only one skater of the four selected was sent to Europe, 19-year-old elevator-boy " [:a {:href "/athletes/98923"} "Tommy White"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Some of the top speed skaters were missing from the Olympics, competing in speed skating races for workers instead. This included competitors from the Soviet Union, which was absent from the entire Games, but also several Norwegians. " [:a {:href "/athletes/96283"} "Haakon Pedersen"] " could rival the top skaters in the two shortest distances, and Trygve Barø had posted the second best time of the season in the 500 metres. Briefly before the Olympics, the Workers European Championships were held in Oslo, with Pedersen winning ahead of Ivan Anikanov and Yakov Melnikov (both USSR, the latter being 40 years old)."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/989"} "500 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "11 February 1936"] "\n" [:td {} "36"] "\n" [:td {} "14"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/990"} "1,500 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "13 February 1936"] "\n" [:td {} "37"] "\n" [:td {} "15"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/991"} "5,000 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "12 